{"step_index":50,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-02T19:13:02Z","content":"Here is the complete, standalone, production-ready Security, Authentication, and Audit Logging module engineered for a law enforcement intelligence system using FastAPI, AES-256-GCM AEAD encryption, and cryptographic hash chains.\n\n### Core Security Architecture\n\n```\n                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                    │               Incoming HTTP Request              │\n                    └─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┘\n                                              │ X-Auth-Token Header\n                                              ▼\n                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                    │  current_user() Dependency                       │\n                    │  - Resolves token in USERS                       │\n                    │  - Returns Principal (401 on failure)            │\n                    └─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┘\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                    │  require(principal, permission)                  │\n                    │  - Evaluates Principal.can(permission)           │\n                    │  - On DENIAL: audit() -> raises 403 Forbidden    │\n                    └─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┘\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                    │  Tamper-Evident Audit Logging                    │\n                    │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n                    │  │ AES-256-GCM Payload Encryption              │ │\n                    │  │ (CNAS_AUDIT_KEY -> 96-bit Nonce + GCM Tag)  │ │\n                    │  └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘ │\n                    │                         ▼                        │\n                    │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n                    │  │ Cryptographic Hash Chain (SHA-256)          │ │\n                    │  │ seq, timestamp, user, detail, prev_hash     │ │\n                    │  │ -> compute entry_hash                       │ │\n                    │  └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────┘ │\n                    │                         ▼                        │\n                    │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n                    │  │ Thread-Safe Append (threading.Lock)         │ │\n                    │  │ -> audit_log.jsonl                          │ │\n                    │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n                    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Complete Standalone Implementation: `security.py`\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport base64\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport threading\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, NamedTuple\n\n# FastAPI imports\nfrom fastapi import Depends, Header, HTTPException, status\n\n# Cryptography AEAD import with graceful fallback\ntry:\n    from cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.aead import AESGCM\n    HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY = True\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover\n    AESGCM = None\n    HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY = False\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# 1. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Authentication\n# =====================================================================\n\nINVESTIGATOR_PERMS: set[str] = {\n    \"graph:read\",\n    \"entity:read\",\n    \"evidence:read\",\n    \"query:run\",\n    \"report:generate\",\n    \"data:submit\",\n}\n\nSUPERVISOR_PERMS: set[str] = INVESTIGATOR_PERMS | {\n    \"audit:read\",\n    \"analytics:tune\",\n}\n\nADMIN_PERMS: set[str] = SUPERVISOR_PERMS | {\n    \"data:ingest\",\n    \"user:manage\",\n}\n\nVIEWER_PERMS: set[str] = {\n    \"graph:read\",\n}\n\nROLES: dict[str, set[str]] = {\n    \"investigator\": INVESTIGATOR_PERMS,\n    \"supervisor\": SUPERVISOR_PERMS,\n    \"admin\": ADMIN_PERMS,\n    \"viewer\": VIEWER_PERMS,\n}\n\nUSERS: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {\n    \"demo-investigator\": {\n        \"name\": \"Det. Sarah Miller\",\n        \"role\": \"investigator\",\n        \"unit\": \"Major Narcotics Task Force\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-7402\",\n    },\n    \"demo-supervisor\": {\n        \"name\": \"Lt. Marcus Vance\",\n        \"role\": \"supervisor\",\n        \"unit\": \"Special Investigations Division\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-3319\",\n    },\n    \"demo-admin\": {\n        \"name\": \"Chief Elena Rostova\",\n        \"role\": \"admin\",\n        \"unit\": \"Intelligence & Cyber Operations\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-1001\",\n    },\n    \"demo-viewer\": {\n        \"name\": \"Analyst David Park\",\n        \"role\": \"viewer\",\n        \"unit\": \"Criminal Intelligence Bureau\",\n        \"badge\": \"BADGE-9082\",\n    },\n}\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Principal:\n    \"\"\"Represents an authenticated law enforcement principal.\"\"\"\n    name: str\n    role: str\n    unit: str\n    badge: str\n    token: str | None = None\n\n    def can(self, permission: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check whether the principal's assigned role grants the requested permission.\"\"\"\n        role_perms = ROLES.get(self.role, set())\n        return permission in role_perms\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, str]:\n        \"\"\"Serialize principal metadata for audit logging.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"name\": self.name,\n            \"role\": self.role,\n            \"unit\": self.unit,\n            \"badge\": self.badge,\n        }\n\n\ndef current_user(x_auth_token: str = Header(..., alias=\"X-Auth-Token\")) -> Principal:\n    \"\"\"\n    FastAPI dependency to extract, validate, and authenticate the Principal\n    from the 'X-Auth-Token' header. Raises HTTP 401 if token is unknown or missing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not x_auth_token or x_auth_token not in USERS:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"Authentication failed: invalid or unrecognized authorization token.\",\n            headers={\"WWW-Authenticate\": \"X-Auth-Token\"},\n        )\n\n    user_info = USERS[x_auth_token]\n    return Principal(\n        name=user_info[\"name\"],\n        role=user_info[\"role\"],\n        unit=user_info[\"unit\"],\n        badge=user_info[\"badge\"],\n        token=x_auth_token,\n    )\n\n\ndef require(principal: Principal, permission: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Enforce that the principal possesses the requested permission.\n    If denied, an audit entry is automatically written to the tamper-evident\n    log and an HTTP 403 Forbidden exception is raised.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not principal.can(permission):\n        # Mandatory audit trail for unauthorized access attempts\n        audit(\n            principal=principal,\n            action=\"auth:permission_denied\",\n            detail={\n                \"attempted_permission\": permission,\n                \"role\": principal.role,\n                \"badge\": principal.badge,\n                \"status\": \"DENIED\",\n                \"reason\": f\"Role '{principal.role}' lacks permission '{permission}'\",\n            },\n        )\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail=f\"Access denied: permission '{permission}' required for role '{principal.role}'.\",\n        )\n\n\ndef require_permission(permission: str) -> Callable[[Principal], Principal]:\n    \"\"\"\n    FastAPI dependency factory for declarative endpoint permission checks.\n    Usage: @app.get('/evidence', dependencies=[Depends(require_permission('evidence:read'))])\n    \"\"\"\n    def _dependency(principal: Principal = Depends(current_user)) -> Principal:\n        require(principal, permission)\n        return principal\n    return _dependency\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# 2. AES-256-GCM At-Rest Encryption\n# =====================================================================\n\nclass EncryptedPayload(NamedTuple):\n    blob: str\n    encrypted: bool\n\n\ndef _get_audit_key() -> bytes | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract a 32-byte (256-bit) encryption key from CNAS_AUDIT_KEY.\n    Supports:\n      1. 64-character hex strings (e.g. from secrets.token_hex(32))\n      2. 44-character base64 encoded strings\n      3. Raw 32-byte UTF-8 character strings\n    Returns None if absent, invalid length, or if the cryptography library is missing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY or AESGCM is None:\n        return None\n\n    raw = os.environ.get(\"CNAS_AUDIT_KEY\")\n    if not raw:\n        return None\n\n    raw = raw.strip()\n\n    # 1. 64-character Hex string\n    if len(raw) == 64:\n        try:\n            key_bytes = bytes.fromhex(raw)\n            if len(key_bytes) == 32:\n                return key_bytes\n        except ValueError:\n            pass\n\n    # 2. Base64 encoded string\n    try:\n        decoded = base64.b64decode(raw, validate=True)\n        if len(decoded) == 32:\n            return decoded\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    # 3. Raw 32-byte UTF-8 string\n    encoded = raw.encode(\"utf-8\")\n    if len(encoded) == 32:\n        return encoded\n\n    return None\n\n\ndef _encrypt(payload: dict[str, Any]) -> EncryptedPayload:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encrypt a payload dictionary using AES-256-GCM (AEAD).\n    Generates a cryptographically random 96-bit (12-byte) nonce per write.\n    Falls back to canonical plaintext JSON if CNAS_AUDIT_KEY or cryptography is unavailable.\n    Returns:\n        EncryptedPayload(blob: str, encrypted: bool)\n    \"\"\"\n    key = _get_audit_key()\n    canonical_json = json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n\n    if key is None or not HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY or AESGCM is None:\n        return EncryptedPayload(blob=canonical_json, encrypted=False)\n\n    # 96-bit GCM nonce (NIST SP 800-38D recommendation)\n    nonce = os.urandom(12)\n    aesgcm = AESGCM(key)\n    # Ciphertext contains encrypted bytes concatenated with the 16-byte authentication tag\n    ciphertext = aesgcm.encrypt(nonce, canonical_json.encode(\"utf-8\"), associated_data=None)\n    # Pack nonce + ciphertext into URL-safe base64 string\n    blob = base64.b64encode(nonce + ciphertext).decode(\"ascii\")\n    return EncryptedPayload(blob=blob, encrypted=True)\n\n\ndef _decrypt(blob: str, encrypted: bool) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decrypt an audit log payload blob.\n    If encrypted is False, parses the blob as JSON.\n    If encrypted is True, decrypts using AES-256-GCM with the key from CNAS_AUDIT_KEY.\n    Raises ValueError if decryption fails, data is tampered, or key is unavailable.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not encrypted:\n        try:\n            return json.loads(blob)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Failed to decode plaintext JSON audit blob: {exc}\") from exc\n\n    key = _get_audit_key()\n    if key is None or not HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY or AESGCM is None:\n        raise ValueError(\n            \"Audit payload is encrypted, but encryption key (CNAS_AUDIT_KEY) \"\n            \"or cryptography library is unavailable.\"\n        )\n\n    try:\n        raw_data = base64.b64decode(blob.encode(\"ascii\"), validate=True)\n        if len(raw_data) < 28:  # 12-byte nonce + 16-byte minimum auth tag\n            raise ValueError(\"Encrypted blob length is insufficient for AES-256-GCM.\")\n        nonce = raw_data[:12]\n        ciphertext_and_tag = raw_data[12:]\n        aesgcm = AESGCM(key)\n        plaintext = aesgcm.decrypt(nonce, ciphertext_and_tag, associated_data=None)\n        return json.loads(plaintext.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n    except Exception as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"AES-256-GCM payload decryption failed: {exc}\") from exc\n\n\ndef encryption_status() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return status metadata for at-rest audit encryption.\n    \"\"\"\n    key = _get_audit_key()\n    key_configured = key is not None\n    active = HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY and key_configured\n    return {\n        \"encryption_active\": active,\n        \"library_available\": HAS_CRYPTOGRAPHY,\n        \"key_configured\": key_configured,\n        \"algorithm\": \"AES-256-GCM\" if active else \"plaintext_fallback\",\n        \"env_var\": \"CNAS_AUDIT_KEY\",\n    }\n\n\n# =====================================================================\n# 3. Tamper-Evident Audit Logging (Hash Chain)\n# =====================================================================\n\nAUDIT_LOG_FILE: Path = Path(\"audit_log.jsonl\")\nGENESIS_PREV_HASH: str = \"0\" * 64\n_LOG_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n\n\ndef _compute_hash(entry: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute a deterministic SHA-256 hash of an entry across all its fields,\n    excluding 'entry_hash' itself. Uses canonical JSON sorting and separators.\n    \"\"\"\n    hashable_data = {k: v for k, v in entry.items() if k != \"entry_hash\"}\n    canonical = json.dumps(hashable_data, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    return hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef audit(\n    principal: Principal | dict[str, Any] | None,\n    action: str,\n    detail: dict[str, Any],\n    log_path: Path | str | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a tamper-evident, cryptographically chained audit log entry.\n    Thread-safe write guarded by threading.Lock().\n    The detail dictionary is encrypted using _encrypt().\n    \"\"\"\n    target_path = Path(log_path) if log_path else AUDIT_LOG_FILE\n\n    # Normalize user details\n    if isinstance(principal, Principal):\n        user_info = principal.to_dict()\n    elif isinstance(principal, dict):\n        user_info = {\n            \"name\": str(principal.get(\"name\", \"Unknown\")),\n            \"role\": str(principal.get(\"role\", \"unknown\")),\n            \"unit\": str(principal.get(\"unit\", \"unknown\")),\n            \"badge\": str(principal.get(\"badge\", \"N/A\")),\n        }\n    else:\n        user_info = {\n            \"name\": \"SYSTEM\",\n            \"role\": \"system\",\n            \"unit\": \"KERNEL\",\n            \"badge\": \"SYS-0000\",\n        }\n\n    # Encrypt the detail payload via AES-256-GCM or plaintext fallback\n    encrypted_payload = _encrypt(detail)\n\n    with _LOG_LOCK:\n        # Determine sequence number and prev_hash from the last record\n        prev_hash = GENESIS_PREV_HASH\n        next_seq = 1\n\n        if target_path.exists() and target_path.stat().st_size > 0:\n            with open(target_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                lines = [line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()]\n                if lines:\n                    last_entry = json.loads(lines[-1])\n                    next_seq = int(last_entry[\"seq\"]) + 1\n                    prev_hash = str(last_entry[\"entry_hash\"])\n\n        timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n        entry_data: dict[str, Any] = {\n            \"seq\": next_seq,\n            \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n            \"action\": action,\n            \"user\": user_info,\n            \"detail\": encrypted_payload.blob,\n            \"encrypted\": encrypted_payload.encrypted,\n            \"prev_hash\": prev_hash,\n        }\n\n        # Calculate the entry's hash over all its core fields\n        entry_hash = _compute_hash(entry_data)\n        entry_data[\"entry_hash\"] = entry_hash\n\n        # Append entry to the JSONL log file\n        with open(target_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(json.dumps(entry_data, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n\n    return entry_data\n\n\ndef read_audit(limit: int = 100, log_path: Path | str | None = None) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Read the latest audit log entries from the JSONL file, decrypting\n    the 'detail' payload for each entry.\n    \"\"\"\n    target_path = Path(log_path) if log_path else AUDIT_LOG_FILE\n    if not target_path.exists():\n        return []\n\n    with _LOG_LOCK:\n        with open(target_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            lines = [line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()]\n\n    target_lines = lines[-limit:] if limit > 0 else []\n    results = []\n\n    for line in target_lines:\n        raw_entry = json.loads(line)\n        blob = raw_entry.get(\"detail\", \"\")\n        encrypted_flag = raw_entry.get(\"encrypted\", False)\n\n        try:\n            decrypted_detail = _decrypt(blob, encrypted_flag)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            decrypted_detail = {\"_decryption_error\": str(exc), \"_raw_blob\": blob}\n\n        entry = dict(raw_entry)\n        entry[\"detail\"] = decrypted_detail\n        results.append(entry)\n\n    return results\n\n\ndef verify_chain(log_path: Path | str | None = None) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Verify cryptographic integrity across the entire JSONL audit trail.\n    Hashes each entry and compares it to the next entry's prev_hash pointer.\n\n    Checks:\n      1. Genesis entry prev_hash == 64 zeros and seq == 1.\n      2. In-place content integrity: entry's recomputed hash matches entry_hash.\n      3. Sequential continuity: next_entry['seq'] == curr_entry['seq'] + 1.\n      4. Chain link: next_entry['prev_hash'] == hash(curr_entry).\n\n    Returns:\n      int: The exact sequence number (seq) of the entry that broke the chain.\n      None: If the chain is completely intact and verified.\n    \"\"\"\n    target_path = Path(log_path) if log_path else AUDIT_LOG_FILE\n    if not target_path.exists():\n        return None\n\n    with _LOG_LOCK:\n        with open(target_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            lines = [line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()]\n\n    if not lines:\n        return None\n\n    entries = [json.loads(line) for line in lines]\n\n    # 1. Verify Genesis Entry\n    genesis = entries[0]\n    if genesis.get(\"seq\") != 1:\n        return genesis.get(\"seq\", 1)\n\n    if genesis.get(\"prev_hash\") != GENESIS_PREV_HASH:\n        return genesis.get(\"seq\", 1)\n\n    if _compute_hash(genesis) != genesis.get(\"entry_hash\"):\n        return genesis.get(\"seq\", 1)\n\n    # 2. Verify each consecutive entry in the chain\n    for i in range(len(entries) - 1):\n        curr_entry = entries[i]\n        next_entry = entries[i + 1]\n\n        curr_computed_hash = _compute_hash(curr_entry)\n\n        # Detect in-place alteration of current entry\n        if curr_computed_hash != curr_entry.get(\"entry_hash\"):\n            return curr_entry.get(\"seq\", i + 1)\n\n        # Detect deletions or out-of-order sequence gaps\n        expected_next_seq = curr_entry.get(\"seq\", 0) + 1\n        if next_entry.get(\"seq\") != expected_next_seq:\n            return expected_next_seq\n\n        # Hash current entry and compare to next entry's prev_hash\n        if curr_computed_hash != next_entry.get(\"prev_hash\"):\n            return curr_entry.get(\"seq\", i + 1)\n\n    # 3. Verify final entry's internal hash integrity\n    last_entry = entries[-1]\n    if _compute_hash(last_entry) != last_entry.get(\"entry_hash\"):\n        return last_entry.get(\"seq\", len(entries))\n\n    return None\n```\n\n---\n\n### Example FastAPI Application Integration\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Depends, Query\nfrom security import (\n    Principal,\n    current_user,\n    require,\n    require_permission,\n    audit,\n    read_audit,\n    verify_chain,\n    encryption_status,\n)\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"Law Enforcement Intelligence & Analytics System\")\n\n@app.get(\"/intel/graph\")\ndef get_intel_graph(user: Principal = Depends(current_user)):\n    \"\"\"Accessible to investigator, supervisor, admin, and viewer.\"\"\"\n    require(user, \"graph:read\")\n    audit(user, \"graph:read\", {\"target\": \"cartel_nexus_v2\"})\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\", \"nodes\": 124, \"edges\": 432}\n\n@app.post(\"/evidence/submit\")\ndef submit_evidence(payload: dict, user: Principal = Depends(require_permission(\"data:submit\"))):\n    \"\"\"Accessible to investigator, supervisor, and admin.\"\"\"\n    audit(user, \"evidence:submit\", {\"case_number\": payload.get(\"case_no\"), \"item_count\": 1})\n    return {\"status\": \"submitted\", \"officer\": user.badge}\n\n@app.get(\"/system/audit\")\ndef view_audit_logs(\n    limit: int = Query(default=20, le=100),\n    user: Principal = Depends(require_permission(\"audit:read\")),\n):\n    \"\"\"Accessible to supervisor and admin.\"\"\"\n    logs = read_audit(limit=limit)\n    return {\"count\": len(logs), \"logs\": logs}\n\n@app.get(\"/system/audit/verify\")\ndef verify_audit_chain(user: Principal = Depends(require_permission(\"audit:read\"))):\n    \"\"\"Cryptographically verifies the audit log hash chain.\"\"\"\n    broken_seq = verify_chain()\n    if broken_seq is not None:\n        return {\n            \"status\": \"ALERT_COMPROMISED\",\n            \"broken_seq\": broken_seq,\n            \"message\": f\"Cryptographic continuity severed at sequence #{broken_seq}\",\n        }\n    return {\n        \"status\": \"SECURE\",\n        \"broken_seq\": None,\n        \"message\": \"Audit chain intact and cryptographically verified\",\n    }\n\n@app.get(\"/system/encryption-status\")\ndef get_status():\n    return encryption_status()\n```\n\n---\n\n### Verification and Edge Case Handling\n\n1. **RBAC & Authorization**:\n   - Investigator role possesses `{graph:read, entity:read, evidence:read, query:run, report:generate, data:submit}`.\n   - Supervisor role inherits investigator permissions and adds `{audit:read, analytics:tune}`.\n   - Admin role inherits supervisor permissions and adds `{data:ingest, user:manage}`.\n   - Viewer role is locked to `{graph:read}`.\n   - Any access denial invokes `audit(...)` with action `\"auth:permission_denied\"` before raising `HTTPException(403)`.\n\n2. **At-Rest Encryption**:\n   - `_get_audit_key()` automatically validates 256-bit keys from `CNAS_AUDIT_KEY` formatted as 64-char Hex, 44-char Base64, or raw 32-byte strings.\n   - If the environment variable is not configured or if `cryptography` is absent, it automatically falls back to canonical plaintext JSON while `encryption_status()` flags `\"encryption_active\": False`.\n\n3. **Tamper-Evident Hash Chain & Concurrency**:\n   - Protected with `threading.Lock()` against race conditions during concurrent requests.\n   - Every record's `entry_hash` is computed over `(seq, timestamp, action, user, detail, encrypted, prev_hash)`.\n   - `verify_chain()` detects in-place record alteration, record deletion (sequence gaps), and link tampering, returning the exact sequence number that compromised the chain.","thinking":"**Verifying function parameter consistency**\n\nThe initial assessment confirms the function signatures align with the given requirement: `_encrypt(payload: dict)` and `_decrypt(blob: str, encrypted: bool)`.\n\nA question arose regarding whether the `_encrypt` function output could be unpacked directly into variables. Positive confirmation shows that this behavior is achievable, as the encrypted result can be unpacked from the return as `blob, encrypted = _encrypt(payload)` or from `res.blob` and `res.encrypted`.\n\n\n"}
